<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xml:lang="en"
      lang="en"
      metal:use-macro="context/main_template/macros/master"
      i18n:domain="senaite.core">
  <head></head>
  <body>
    <metal:main fill-slot="main">
      <article id="content">
        <h1 class="documentFirstHeading"
            i18n:translate="title_sharing_disabled">
          Sharing is disabled here
        </h1>

        <div class="alert alert-info" role="alert">
          <p i18n:translate="description_sharing_disabled_intro">
            Access to a client and everything it contains is granted
            automatically when a contact under that client is linked
            to a user account. There is no need to assign roles or
            users on this page.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 i18n:translate="title_sharing_disabled_how_it_works">
          How access is granted
        </h2>

        <p i18n:translate="description_sharing_disabled_mechanism">
          The user property
          <code i18n:name="property">linked_client_uid</code>
          carries the UID of the client a user is linked to. A
          dynamic local-role provider on every client-tree object
          checks that property at request time and grants the
          <strong i18n:name="owner">Owner</strong> and
          <strong i18n:name="client">Client</strong> roles on the
          fly when it matches. No persistent local role is written
          on the client folder, and no recursive security reindex
          runs when contacts come and go.
        </p>

        <h2 i18n:translate="title_sharing_disabled_how_to_grant">
          To grant access to a user
        </h2>

        <ol>
          <li i18n:translate="description_sharing_disabled_step1">
            Create a Contact under the client.
          </li>
          <li i18n:translate="description_sharing_disabled_step2">
            Open the contact's Login Details and link an existing
            user account (or create a new one).
          </li>
          <li i18n:translate="description_sharing_disabled_step3">
            The user can now see and edit the client's content
            immediately. Unlinking the contact revokes access just
            as quickly.
          </li>
        </ol>

        <p>
          <a tal:attributes="href context/absolute_url"
             class="btn btn-secondary"
             i18n:translate="button_back_to_client">
            Back to client
          </a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </metal:main>
  </body>
</html>
